BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Celebration Ensemble: A Tribute Concert Featuring "Harvest" by
  Neil Young - Fundraiser
DTSTART:20261024T223000Z
DTEND:20261025T020000Z
DTSTAMP:20261023T141245Z
UID:8e2c632a21e0d1622341431989079929dc5c715a@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Music,Causes
DESCRIPTION:Event by Tioga Arts Council\, Michael Wu and The Celebration E
 nsemble\nOwego Elks 1039\n233 Front St\, Owego\, NY\nPublic\nTioga Arts Co
 uncil (TAC) and The Celebration Ensemble are pleased to present A Tribute 
 Concert Featuring "Harvest" by Neil Young Fundraiser on Saturday\, October
  24\, 2026\, at the Owego Elks Lodge\, 223 Front St.\, Owego.\n.\nCONCERT 
 DETAILS\n• Who: The Celebration Ensemble\n• What: Harvest by Neil Youn
 g\n• Where: Owego Elks Lodge\, 223 Front St.\, Owego\, NY\n• When: Sat
 urday\, October 24\, doors open at 6:30 p.m.\n.\nTICKETS\n• Online At: h
 ttp://weblink.donorperfect.com/celebration-ensemble-2026\n• $20 Pre-Orde
 r Tickets\n• $25 VIP Seated Pre-Order Tickets (Only 100 available)\n• 
 $30 Day-Of Tickets\n.\nTHE CELEBRATION ENSEMBLE - BAND MEMBERS\n1. Cory Ca
 ruso - drums & percussion\n2. Mandy Goldman (Noon Fifteen) - vocals\n3. Sa
 muel B. Lupowitz (Noon Fifteen\, The Pocket Bandits) - keys\, vocals\n4. P
 aul Shotwell - (Front & Main) vocals\n5. Mary Tewksbury (Next To Kin\, Fro
 nt & Main) – guitars\, vocals\n6. Brian Tyneway (Front & Main)- guitars
 \, vocals\n7. Michael Wu (Gunpoets\, Front & Main) - musical director\, vo
 cals\, bass\n.\nOPENING ACT\nThe Bleeding Hearts (Alyssa Brigiotta and Joe
  Kollar)\n.\nPROCEEDS\n• Tickets are non-refundable\, and all sales are 
 final.\n• This is a fundraiser concert\, and all net proceeds benefit Ti
 oga Arts Council (TAC) a 501(c)(3) arts and culture nonprofit and the cent
 ral platform for the arts in Tioga County\, NY.\n• Please consider inqui
 ring about sponsorship opportunities by emailing tiogaartscouncil@gmail.co
 m or purchasing tickets to support this event.\n.\nABOUT THE CELEBRATION E
 NSEMBLE\nThe Celebration Ensemble is a group of musicians from the Ithaca-
 Binghamton regions of New York State who together perform tribute shows to
  celebrate their favorite artists.\n.\nSays Michael Wu\, "It's great to pa
 rtner once again with the Tioga Arts Council to perform another tribute sh
 ow and fundraiser.\n.\n"The spirit of The Celebration Ensemble is communit
 y-oriented. We're all from this rich community in the Southern Tier and Fi
 nger Lakes regions\, and we love getting to highlight the artistic talent 
 around us while paying tribute to the music that shaped us.\n.\n"We really
  enjoy the process of getting a set as tight and true to the original as w
 e can. We want people to hear these songs the way they remember them\, and
  enjoy playing them just as much as the audience enjoys hearing them.\n.\n
 "Everyone in the group performs on most of the songs\, but it's important 
 to me that each member gets a spotlight moment somewhere in the show.\n.\n
 "We always keep the artist under wraps until about six weeks out. Half the
  fun is watching people try to guess. Mark the date\, we'll see you there.
 "\n.\nTo learn more about The Celebration Ensemble\, go to: www.facebook.c
 om/The-Celebration-Ensemble-1312330742256977\n.\nABOUT TIOGA ARTS COUNCIL
 \nThe Tioga Arts Council enriches the cultural lives of residents and visi
 tors by initiating and facilitating creative opportunities and collaborati
 ons. Through exhibitions\, performances\, education and cultural experienc
 es\, the Tioga Arts Council provides a central platform for a creative com
 munity. Our vision is to inspire and support a vibrant\, creative communit
 y in and around Tioga County\, NY. Three values guide our mission\, vision
 \, and programs\, and they are:\n.\n• To Serve the Arts\n• To Serve Th
 rough the Arts\n• To Make the Arts Accessible\n.\nContact Christina Di S
 tefano at tiogaartscouncil@gmail.com if you have additional questions.\n\n
 Source: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78466443/202
 61024183000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78466443/20261024183000
END:VEVENT
