BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Haunted History in Downtown Ithaca
DTSTART:20261029T220000Z
DTEND:20261030T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20261023T141245Z
UID:ff7c31571169f8fd4d64227f14b17810087c1c68@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:History & Heritage
DESCRIPTION:Event by The History Center in Tompkins County\n110 North Tiog
 a Street within the Tompkins Center for History & Culture\, Ithaca\, NY\nP
 ublic\nDowntown Ithaca has seen its share of murder\, disaster\, and thing
 s nobody ever quite explained. On this walking tour\, guides .Sherri La To
 rre and Ben Sandberg and a cast of costumed volunteers take you past the l
 andmarks where real crimes and tragedies left their mark on the city. You'
 ll hear true stories of murder\, jealousy\, and insanity pulled straight f
 rom The History Center's archives\, and come face to face with some of the
  most haunted items in our collection.\nWhat: 75 minute walking tour over 
 sidewalks\, gravel paths\, and grass - with a slight incline.\nWhere: The 
 History Center in Tompkins County\, 110 N Tioga St\, Ithaca NY 14850\nWho:
  This tour is designed for ages 16-116\nWhen:\nTWO TOURS PER DATE:\n* Tour
  1 is 6pm-7:15pm\n* Tour 2 is 7:30-8:45pm\nWear Comfortable Shoes\, Bring 
 an Umbrella\, Jacket\, and Water Bottle\nWeather - this tour takes place r
 ain or shine! In case of severe weather\, we’ll determine cancellations 
 by 10:30 am the morning-of.\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.time
 .ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78493688/20261017180000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78493688/20261017180000
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Evening with Edgar Allan Poe - "Deep Into That Darkness Peering
 " - at Rye\, Elmira
DTSTART:20261029T230000Z
DTEND:20261030T013000Z
DTSTAMP:20261023T141245Z
UID:f30dfd50d5fe2511107f4debd7282fc4a4a3ea04@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Art,Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:An Evening with Edgar Allan Poe: Deep Into That Darkness Peeri
 ng\nOctober 28 & 29\, 7-9:30pm\nIn Support of The ARTS Council of the Sout
 hern Finger Lakes\nJoin The ARTS Council of the Southern Finger Lakes (The
  ARTS Council) and RYE Bar in collaboration with Tim Collins for\, An Even
 ing with Edgar Allan Poe: Deep Into That Darkness Peering.\nStep into the 
 strange and macabre world of Edgar Allan Poe\, brought to life by award-wi
 nning solo performer Tim Collins. Set the stage with us at RYE Bar in Elmi
 ra\, NY for a hauntingly beautiful atmosphere\, a deliciously themed 3-cou
 rse meal\, and cocktails that will send chills down your spine. Sit back\,
  and relax (if you can)\, and let the stories and poetry of Poe whisk you 
 away to another world\, a world of dark secrets and dark nights. Two of Po
 e's most well-known pieces\, The Raven and The Tell-Tale Heart will be per
 formed this year\, as well as some of his lesser-known works.\nA perfect w
 ay to spend the days before Halloween\, your ticket includes a fabulous 3-
 course meal prepared by RYE Bar\, as well as the Poe performance. Themed c
 ocktails will be available at an additional cost.\nCome dressed in your be
 st Halloween and Poe attire! There will be a costume contest with cash pri
 zes for the best 3 costumes of the evening!\nGeneral Seating Tickets are $
 65. Please include the names of the people you would like to sit with if n
 ot purchasing tickets together. We will do our best to accommodate seating
  requests.\nVIP Tickets are $100. Only 4 VIP tickets will be sold for each
  performance. Ticket price includes your meal\, one drink ticket\, priorit
 y seating\, a swag bag\, and professional photo with Poe after the perform
 ance.\nThis event is suggested for ages 12+.\nTickets can be purchased at 
 https://bit.ly/PoeShow2026\nThis event is a fundraiser for The ARTS Counci
 l of the Southern Finger Lakes and features all local actors\, chefs\, foo
 d\, producers\, and collaborators. We are not affiliated with the travelin
 g Poe Speakeasy.\nMade possible with support from The Newbury Giving Fund.
 \nPhoto courtesy of Victoria Scott.\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calen
 dar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78486429/20261028190000
GEO:42.089632;-76.815264
LOCATION:Rye Bar & Restaurant\, 365 Davis Street\, Elmira\, New York\, 149
 01\, United States
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78486429/20261028190000
END:VEVENT
