BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Rachel S. Thaler Concert Piano Series presents Hélène Grimau
 d\, piano
DTSTART:20261104T000000Z
DTEND:20261104T045959Z
DTSTAMP:20261023T141245Z
UID:2415a68894b83292cee1e211f2732461c57f8811@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Music
DESCRIPTION:Tickets are required for this event. To reserve your FREE tick
 ets\, please visit:\nhttps://www.purplepass.com/events/388525-the-rachel-s
 -thaler-concert-pianist-series-presents-helene-grimaud-nov-3rd-2026\nRenai
 ssance woman Hélène Grimaud is not only a passionate pianist who perform
 s with profound poetic expression and incomparable technical mastery. She 
 is equally distinguished as a committed environmentalist\, a compassionate
  human rights advocate\, and an author. Her dedication to music is mirrore
 d by the breadth and depth of her engagement with environmental protection
 \, literature\, and the arts.\nBorn in Aix-en-Provence\, Hélène Grimaud 
 studied with Jacqueline Courtin and Pierre Barbizet in Marseille. At 13\, 
 she was accepted into the Paris Conservatoire\, and in 1987 she gave her d
 ebut recital in Tokyo. That same year\, Daniel Barenboim invited her to pe
 rform with the Orchestre de Paris\, marking the beginning of her career.\n
 In 1995\, she made her debut with the Berlin Philharmonic under Claudio Ab
 bado\, followed by her appearance with the New York Philharmonic under Kur
 t Masur in 1999. Her environmental commitment led her to found the Wolf Co
 nservation Center in Upper New York State. She is also a member of Musicia
 ns for Human Rights and has authored four books\, published in several lan
 guages.\nIn the 2026/2027 season\, under the title “The Last Testament\,
 ” Grimaud devotes herself to the final sonatas of Ludwig van Beethoven a
 nd Franz Schubert\, featuring Beethoven’s Piano Sonata No. 32 in C minor
 \, Op. 111\, and Schubert’s Piano Sonata No. 21 in B-flat major\, D 960.
 \nHer recordings have received numerous awards\, including the Cannes Clas
 sical Recording of the Year\, Diapason d’or\, and ECHO Klassik. She was 
 appointed a Knight of the Légion d’honneur\, France’s highest order o
 f merit.\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/
 78496291/20261103190000
GEO:42.421022;-76.495805
LOCATION:Ford Hall at Ithaca College\, 146 Conservatory Drive\, Ithaca\, N
 ew York\, 14850\, United States
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78496291/20261103190000
END:VEVENT
